s on the off chance that a middleware further up the chain still expect access to the form data. \\n\\nWhat about making it configurable with an Option, with the default behavior being to clean it up. That way the user can have more control over which middleware cleans up the form data.\\n\\nI don't want to stall this issue further but just a thought.\\n\\ncc. @flc1125 @dmathieu  \\n\\n---\\n\\n**flc1125** — 2025-11-10T01:53:34Z\\n\\n> Sorry just got caught up on this thread. My only concern with RemoveAll is on the off chance that a middleware further up the chain still expect access to the form data.\\n\\nAgree.\\n\\n> What about making it configurable with an Option, with the default behavior being to clean it up. That way the user can have more control over which middleware cleans up the form data.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"we should also decid whether to fix this in otelgin onli or to review other middlewar and address the issu there a well if it exist flc1125 2025 11 04t00 35 28z let s reach an agreement on how we should fix it we tend to onli need to add the follow on the basi of the origin main branch go c request multipartform removeal we should also decid whether to fix this in otelgin onli or to review other middlewar and address the issu there a well if it exist in fact all middlewar base on http request ha issu whenev a situat like c request withcontext c request context occur so other compon also need to be fix howev for this current pr we onli need to fix otelgin to keep the pr a minim a possibl for other middlewar if you are interest you can also submit fix in the form of minim pr for individu compon yile j 2025 11 04t01 19 00z flc1125 removeal work for me i think my origin pr alreadi align well with the goal it look like i just need to resolv the conflict and make sure the test pas let me confirm agin that we re all in agreement on this approach dmathieu akats7 akats7 2025 11 10t01 45 42z sorri just got caught up on this thread my onli concern with removeal is on the off chanc that a middlewar further up the chain still expect access to the form data what about make it configur with an option with the default behavior be to clean it up that way the user can have more control over which middlewar clean up the form data i don t want to stall this issu further but just a thought cc flc1125 dmathieu flc1125 2025 11 10t01 53 34z sorri just got caught up on this thread my onli concern with removeal is on the off chanc that a middlewar further up the chain still expect access to the form data agre what about make it configur with an option with the default behavior be to clean it up that way the user can have more control over which middlewar clean up the form data\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"id\": \"3c8bf7e7b452e3f2\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3174232500062194, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.11869052572317056, \"vector_similarity\": 0.78113294, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 27213, \"chunk_count\": 18, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:09\", \"token_count\": 9176, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"    gin2_test.go:33: File modified: /var/folders/9q/lfpvvb251dv7bj4tqlq8bgpm0000gn/T/TestHTTP124433030/001/multipart-643567324\\n\\n    gin2_test.go:33: File modified: /var/folders/9q/lfpvvb251dv7bj4tqlq8bgpm0000gn/T/TestHTTP124433030/001/multipart-643567324\\n\\n    gin2_test.go:33: File modified: /var/folders/9q/lfpvvb251dv7bj4tqlq8bgpm0000gn/T/TestHTTP124433030/001/multipart-643567324\\n\\n    gin2_test.go:36: File removed: /var/folders/9q/lfpvvb251dv7bj4tqlq8bgpm0000gn/T/TestHTTP124433030/001/multipart-643567324\\n\\n```\\n\\n----\\n\\nCurrently, I cannot determine whether this is a flaw in Go itself or if users are required to manually execute `RemoveAll()`. I have tried submitting [this issue](https://github.com/golang/go/issues/74455) to the official Go team to see if there will be any updates.\\n\\nThe following situations exist (tested and confirmed):\\n\\n1. We executed `request.WithContext()` before executing `request.ParseMultipartForm`, but did not manually call `RemoveAll` on the new Request—it will be unable to delete the files;\\n\\n2. We executed `request.WithContext()` before executing `request.ParseMultipartForm`, and manually called `RemoveAll` on the new Request—it will delete the files;\\n\\n3. We executed `request.WithContext()` after executing `request.ParseMultipartForm,` and did not manually call `RemoveAll` on the new Request—it will delete the files.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**flc1125** — 2025-07-03T13:24:52Z\\n\\nGiven that this [issue](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/5946#issuecomment-3028290240) currently lacks an official solution from the [Go team](https://github.com/golang/go/issues/74455), we need to find an appropriate workaround ourselves.\\n\\nMy suggestion is to proceed with the solution proposed in this [PR](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/6609) (also the consistent approach suggested by @zihuyishi and @akats7).  \\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"gin2 _ test go 33 file modifi var folder 9q lfpvvb251dv7bj4tqlq8bgpm0000gn t testhttp124433030 001 multipart 643567324 gin2 _ test go 33 file modifi var folder 9q lfpvvb251dv7bj4tqlq8bgpm0000gn t test