entelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8751eb948a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 16121, \"chunk_count\": 10, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:14\", \"token_count\": 5002, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"However, this approach will also introduce additional side effects, for which there is currently no better solution.  \\n\\n**Impact:**  \\n\\nAssuming our middleware is wrapped in the following manner: `m1(m2(otel-middleware(m3(fn))))`,  \\n\\nwhere `m1` and `m2` internally implement operations such as `request.ParseMultipartForm(1)`. Due to the effect of `RemoveAll` in `otel-middleware`,  \\n\\nthere may be cases where they repeatedly create `request.MultipartForm` resources, resulting in additional memory allocations.\\n\\nOf course, we can also choose not to handle it, but we need to remind users to process `c.Request.MultipartForm.RemoveAll()`.\\n\\n----\\n\\nI'd like to hear your opinions: @akats7 @open-telemetry/go-approvers \\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-ISSUE-01]\\n\\n# Issue: Using otelgin.Middleware will cause temporary MultipartForm files not to be destroyed. (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#5946)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/5946  \\n\\n**Author**: zacklpx  \\n\\n**Created**: 2024-07-25T03:50:39Z · **Updated**: 2025-07-03T13:28:05Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: open  \\n\\n**Labels**: bug, area: instrumentation, instrumentation: otelgin  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Timeline\\n\\n- 2024-07-25T03:50:39Z · **labeled** by zacklpx `area: instrumentation`\\n\\n- 2024-07-25T03:50:39Z · **labeled** by zacklpx `bug`\\n\\n- 2024-07-25T03:50:39Z · **labeled** by zacklpx `instrumentation: otelgin`\\n\\n- 2024-11-21T12:21:58Z · **cross-referenced** by flc1125 ← https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/4588\\n\\n- 2025-01-13T13:45:45Z · **cross-referenced** by Yiling-J ← https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/6609\\n\\n- 2025-07-02T08:06:05Z · **marked_as_duplicate** by dmathieu\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"howev this approach will also introduc addit side effect for which there is current no better solut impact assum our middlewar is wrap in the follow manner m1 m2 otel middlewar m3 fn where m1 and m2 intern implement oper such a request parsemultipartform 1 due to the effect of removeal in otel middlewar there may be case where they repeat creat request multipartform resourc result in addit memori alloc of cours we can also choos not to handl it but we need to remind user to process c request multipartform removeal i d like to hear your opinion akats7 open telemetri go approv sourc id src issu 01 issu use otelgin middlewar will caus temporari multipartform file not to be destroy open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 5946 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 5946 author zacklpx creat 2024 07 25t03 50 39z updat 2025 07 03t13 28 05z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state open label bug area instrument instrument otelgin mileston timelin 2024 07 25t03 50 39z label by zacklpx area instrument 2024 07 25t03 50 39z label by zacklpx bug 2024 07 25t03 50 39z label by zacklpx instrument otelgin 2024 11 21t12 21 58z cross referenc by flc1125 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 4588 2025 01 13t13 45 45z cross referenc by yile j http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 6609 2025 07 02t08 06 05z mark _ a _ duplic by dmathieu\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8751eb948a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"id\": \"5b39be36d40588b5\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3060761496819908, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.11372962811712978, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7548847, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8751eb948a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 16121, \"chunk_count\": 10, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:14\", \"token_count\": 5002, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"=== RUN   TestIssue_Middleware\\n\\n    issue_test.go:55: req0.0: 0x140001b6500, req.URL: 0x14000130360\\n\\n    issue_test.go:15: req1.0: 0x140001b6500, req.URL: 0x14000130360\\n\\n    issue_test.go:20: req2.0: 0x140001b6500, req.URL: 0x14000130360\\n\\n    issue_test.go:30: req2.1: 0x140001b6640, req.URL: 0x14000130360\\n\\n    issue_test.go:34: req2.2: 0x140001b6640, req.URL: 0x140001303f0\\n\\n    issue_test.go:24: req2.3: 0x140001b6640, req.URL: 0x140001303f0\\n\\n    issue_test.go:26: req2.4: 0x140001b6780, req.URL: 0x140001303f0\\n\\n    issue_test.go:43: req3.0: 0x140001b6640, req.URL: 0x140001303f0\\n\\n    issue_test.go:44: req3.1: value\\n\\n--- PASS: TestIssue_Middleware (0.00s)\\n\\nPASS\\n\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Yiling-J** — 2025-01-14T15:29:23Z\\n\\nI skipped the failed test on the Windows platform. This is consistent with how Go handles form cleanup tests (https://github.com/golang/go/blob/6da16013ba4444e0d71540f68279f0283a92d05d/src/net/http/serve_test.go#L7028), so I think it’s fine.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**flc1125** — 2025-11-03T13:01:49Z\\n\\n@Yiling-J Hi, are you still willing to handle this issue?\\n\\nAccording to the SIG discussion, it is recommended that middleware remove temporary resources.\\n\\ncc @akats7 \\n\\n---\\n\\n**Yiling-J** — 2025-11-03T15:41:21Z\\n\\n> are you still willing to handle this issue\\n\\n@flc1125 Yes. But first, let’s reach an agreement on how we should fix it. As I proposed a while ago, I prefer the reattach approach: “copy the cloned `Request.MultipartForm` value back to the original request before returning,” as mentioned in https://github.com/golang/go/issues/74455#issuecomment-3099652232.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"run testissu _ middlewar issu _ test go 55 req0 0 0x140001b6500 req url 0x14000130360 issu _ test go 15 req1 0 0x140001b6500 req url 0x14000130360 issu _ test go 20 req2 0 0x140001b6500 req url 0x14000130360 issu _ test go 30 req2 1 0x140001b6640 req url 0x14000130360 issu _ test go 34 req2 2 0x140001b6640 req url 0x140001303f0 issu _ test go 24 req2 3 0x140001b6640 req url 0x140001303f0 issu _ test go 26 req2 4 0x140001b6780 req url 0x140001303f0 issu _ test go 43 req3 0 0x140001b6640 req url 0x140001303f0 issu _ test go 44 req3 1 valu pas testissu _ middlewar 0 00s pas yile j 2025 01 14t15 29 23z i skip the fail test on the window platform this is consist with how go handl form cleanup test http github com golang go blob 6da16013ba4444e0d71540f68279f0283a92d05d src net http serv _ test go l7028 so i think it s fine flc1125 2025 11 03t13 01 49z yile j hi are you still will to handl this issu accord to the sig discuss it is recommend that middlewar remov temporari resourc cc akats7 yile j 2025 11 03t15 41 21z are you still will to handl this issu flc1125 yes but first let s reach an agreement on how we should fix it a i propos a while ago i prefer the reattach approach copi the clone request multipartform valu back to the origin request befor return a mention in http github com golang go issu 74455 issuecom 3099652232\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"id\": \"168d6f7543eb6616\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.30412538432233244, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.09758684188904636, \"vector_similarity\": 0.78604865, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 27213, \"chunk_count\": 18, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:09\", \"token_count\": 9176, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"I don’t think this is the expected result; in any case—whether it’s middleware or something else—it should be able to retrieve the file again.\\n\\nI think we may need to investigate this issue further.\\n\\n**flc1125** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin_test.go` (line 512) — 2025-11-11T13:59:33Z\\n\\nBased on this PR, I’ve provided a prototype reference: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8161\\n\\n@dmathieu @akats7, take a look and see how it works if we adjust it according to the prototype.\\n\\n**akats7** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin_test.go` (line 512) — 2025-11-11T15:42:57Z\\n\\n@flc1125 can you clarify which behavior you’re referring to as incorrect, are you referring to \\n\\n```\\n\\nrequire.ErrorIs(t, err, fs.ErrNotExist)\\n\\n```\\n\\n**Yiling-J** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin_test.go` (line 512) — 2025-11-12T01:28:14Z\\n\\nI thought we had already agreed on the `RemoveAll` approach? Naturally, if you call RemoveAll, the temporary files are deleted and can’t be accessed afterward. Since this happens during the middleware’s return phase, I’d expect that most middlewares wouldn’t read the multipart form at that point anyway. I’m not sure if the implications of RemoveAll were discussed in the SIG meeting, but it might be worth confirming.\\n\\n**akats7** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin_test.go` (line 512) — 2025-11-12T10:24:52Z\\n\\n@flc1125 I’m still not clear on the result you’re referring to, the result aligns to my understanding of what we’ve discussed.\\n\\nAlso I’m not sure if your prototype fix would work, I think it still doesn’t address the core issue which is that when we originally set c.Request = c.Request.WithContext(ctx) with an unparsed form the http server won’t know to clean it up. I don’t think Cloning the request solves that.\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-01]\\n\\n# Pull Request: fix(otelgin): remove multipartform temporary file (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#6609)\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"i don t think this is the expect result in ani case whether it s middlewar or someth els it should be abl to retriev the file again i think we may need to investig this issu further flc1125 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin _ test go line 512 2025 11 11t13 59 33z base on this pr i ve provid a prototyp refer http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8161 dmathieu akats7 take a look and see how it work if we adjust it accord to the prototyp akats7 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin _ test go line 512 2025 11 11t15 42 57z flc1125 can you clarifi which behavior you re refer to a incorrect are you refer to requir errori t err f errnotexist yile j on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin _ test go line 512 2025 11 12t01 28 14z i thought we had alreadi agre on the removeal approach natur if you call removeal the temporari file are delet and can t be access afterward sinc this happen dure the middlewar s return phase i d expect that most middlewar wouldn t read the multipart form at that point anyway i m not sure if the implic of removeal were discuss in the sig meet but it might be worth confirm akats7 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin _ test go line 512 2025 11 12t10 24 52z flc1125 i m still not clear on the result you re refer to the result align to my understand of what we ve discuss also i m not sure if your prototyp fix would work i think it still doesn t address the core issu which is that when we origin set c request c request withcontext ctx with an unpars form the http server won t know to clean it up i don t think clone the request solv that sourc id src pr 01 pull request fix otelgin remov multipartform temporari file open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 6609\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"id\": \"ee5caba072c6dc26\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.29793941894424814, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.08505915706321165, \"vector_similarity\": 0.79466003, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 27213, \"chunk_count\": 18, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:09\", \"token_count\": 9176, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Yiling-J** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/test/gintrace_test.go` — 2025-01-13T15:31:16Z\\n\\nI prefer using `require.NoError` because it ensures that no additional information distracts me when a test has already failed. I also searched the codebase and seems that both `require` and `assert` are used, and `require.NoError` appears more.\\n\\n**Yiling-J** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 117) — 2025-01-13T15:35:44Z\\n\\nIt's hard to say, but in all cases, regardless of how many middlewares are chained, temporary files should be removed. I didn't check the return error of `RemoveAll` here, which aligns with the behavior in both Go's [`http` package](https://github.com/golang/go/blob/44a6f817ea0fbeb3ba4aa398794c4e80dba13b1e/src/net/http/server.go#L1727) and [echo-contrib](https://github.com/labstack/echo-contrib/pull/90). I believe each middleware should independently attempt to remove temporary files.\\n\\n**flc1125** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 117) — 2025-01-13T16:20:13Z\\n\\nsee: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/6609#issuecomment-2587572600\\n\\n**dmathieu** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gintrace.go` — 2025-01-14T08:12:17Z\\n\\nRather than ignoring an error here, how about passing it to the otel error handler?\\n\\n```suggestion\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t\\terr := c.Request.MultipartForm.RemoveAll()\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tif err != nil {\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\totel.Handle(err)\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\n```\\n\\n**dmathieu** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/test/gintrace_test.go` — 2025-01-14T08:13:50Z\\n\\nI think what @flc1125 meant here is that you don't necessarily need to use `AbortWithError` (which also can return an error but ignores it), but instead call `require.NoError` here.\\n\\n```suggestion\\n\\n\\t\\trequire.NoError(err)\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"yile j on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin test gintrac _ test go 2025 01 13t15 31 16z i prefer use requir noerror becaus it ensur that no addit inform distract me when a test ha alreadi fail i also search the codebas and seem that both requir and assert are use and requir noerror appear more yile j on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 117 2025 01 13t15 35 44z it s hard to say but in all case regardless of how mani middlewar are chain temporari file should be remov i didn t check the return error of removeal here which align with the behavior in both go s http packag http github com golang go blob 44a6f817ea0fbeb3ba4aa398794c4e80dba13b1e src net http server go l1727 and echo contrib http github com labstack echo contrib pull 90 i believ each middlewar should independ attempt to remov temporari file flc1125 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 117 2025 01 13t16 20 13z see http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 6609 issuecom 2587572600 dmathieu on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gintrac go 2025 01 14t08 12 17z rather than ignor an error here how about pass it to the otel error handler suggest err c request multipartform removeal if err nil otel handl err dmathieu on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin test gintrac _ test go 2025 01 14t08 13 50z i think what flc1125 meant here is that you don t necessarili need to use abortwitherror which also can return an error but ignor it but instead call requir noerror here suggest requir noerror err\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"id\": \"a6289f2135157364\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2954348742174874, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.09767092031069624, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7568841, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 27213, \"chunk_count\": 18, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:09\", \"token_count\": 9176, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"```\\n\\n**dmathieu** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-14T08:21:31Z\\n\\nWouldn't we be fixing this rather more easily with the following:\\n\\n```suggestion\\n\\n\\t\\tc.Request = c.Request.Clone(ctx)\\n\\n```\\n\\n[WithContext](https://pkg.go.dev/net/http#Request.WithContext) performs a shallow clone, and therefore doesn't clone the multipart form.\\n\\nHowever, [Clone](https://pkg.go.dev/net/http#Request.Clone) performs a deep copy, and makes an explicit clone of [MultipartForm](https://cs.opensource.google/go/go/+/refs/tags/go1.23.4:src/net/http/request.go;l=406).\\n\\n**Yiling-J** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-14T14:39:53Z\\n\\nThe problem here is, go http request will call MultipartForm.RemoveAll() automatically when request finishes. However, the otelgin middleware creates a new request, and temporary files will be stored in this new request's MultipartForm field. Unfortunately, no one is calling MultipartForm.RemoveAll() on this new request.\\n\\nA deep clone wouldn’t resolve the problem because the MultipartForm is also copied. A shallow clone might seem like it should work since the MultipartForm field is shared, but it doesn’t. This is because the MultipartForm field is lazily initialized—it’s only assigned a value when you [parse the form](https://github.com/golang/go/blob/6da16013ba4444e0d71540f68279f0283a92d05d/src/net/http/request.go#L1403). As a result, in the middleware, the field is nil.\\n\\nRelated issues: https://github.com/golang/go/issues/58809, https://github.com/labstack/echo/issues/2413\\n\\nI think other OpenTelemetry middlewares, such as otelmux and otelehco, might also have the same issue.\\n\\n**dmathieu** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-14T14:55:45Z\\n\\nWhat if we parse the form before making the new request?\\n\\nWouldn't we share the object then?\\n\\n**Yiling-J** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-14T15:31:10Z\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"dmathieu on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 14t08 21 31z wouldn t we be fix this rather more easili with the follow suggest c request c request clone ctx withcontext http pkg go dev net http request withcontext perform a shallow clone and therefor doesn t clone the multipart form howev clone http pkg go dev net http request clone perform a deep copi and make an explicit clone of multipartform http c opensourc googl go go ref tag go1 23 4 src net http request go l 406 yile j on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 14t14 39 53z the problem here is go http request will call multipartform removeal automat when request finish howev the otelgin middlewar creat a new request and temporari file will be store in this new request s multipartform field unfortun no one is call multipartform removeal on this new request a deep clone wouldn t resolv the problem becaus the multipartform is also copi a shallow clone might seem like it should work sinc the multipartform field is share but it doesn t this is becaus the multipartform field is lazili initi it s onli assign a valu when you pars the form http github com golang go blob 6da16013ba4444e0d71540f68279f0283a92d05d src net http request go l1403 a a result in the middlewar the field is nil relat issu http github com golang go issu 58809 http github com labstack echo issu 2413 i think other opentelemetri middlewar such a otelmux and otelehco might also have the same issu dmathieu on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 14t14 55 45z what if we pars the form befor make the new request wouldn t we share the object then yile j on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 14t15 31 10z\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"id\": \"0b66ff59ca7469a0\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.29355159494424815, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.08505915706321165, \"vector_similarity\": 0.78003395, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 27213, \"chunk_count\": 18, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:09\", \"token_count\": 9176, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"I think this approach could work, but it feels a bit unusual to enforce form parsing in the middleware.\\n\\n**dmathieu** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-14T16:18:27Z\\n\\nHaving to force remove multipart files is a bit unusual too.\\n\\n**akats7** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-14T17:44:13Z\\n\\nI'm probably more in favor of doing the initialization on the original request as well, explicitly handling clean up logic does seem a bit strange\\n\\n**akats7** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-14T17:49:47Z\\n\\n@dmathieu maybe we should discuss this in the SIG since it might have implications in the other instrumentation modules\\n\\n**dmathieu** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-14T17:50:46Z\\n\\nI won't be able to attend this week's meeting (it's the week where it's late for EU). But yes, feel free to bring it there.\\n\\n**akats7** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-19T18:17:34Z\\n\\n@Yiling-J what are you thoughts on parsing the form in the middleware, the more I think about it, the more that seems to be the better approach, for example what about certain edge cases where down the chain middlewares might want to access the files\\n\\n**Yiling-J** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-20T01:52:04Z\\n\\n@akats7 Another option is to save `c.Request` to a variable before calling `c.Request.WithContext(ctx)`. Then, in the defer function, if `c.Request.MultipartForm != nil`, we can reattach the `MultipartForm` to the original request. This way, there won’t be any automatic removing or parsing. If other middlewares handle the form correctly, this approach should work. \\n\\nIn [http/server.go](https://github.com/golang/go/blob/40b3c0e58a0ae8dec4684a009bf3806769e0fc41/src/net/http/server.go#L2102), the `ServeHTTP` method is called first, which invokes the Gin handlers/middlewares, and then `finishRequest` is called, which removes the temporary files.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"i think this approach could work but it feel a bit unusu to enforc form pars in the middlewar dmathieu on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 14t16 18 27z have to forc remov multipart file is a bit unusu too akats7 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 14t17 44 13z i m probabl more in favor of do the initi on the origin request a well explicit handl clean up logic doe seem a bit strang akats7 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 14t17 49 47z dmathieu mayb we should discus this in the sig sinc it might have implic in the other instrument modul dmathieu on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 14t17 50 46z i won t be abl to attend this week s meet it s the week where it s late for eu but yes feel free to bring it there akats7 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 19t18 17 34z yile j what are you thought on pars the form in the middlewar the more i think about it the more that seem to be the better approach for exampl what about certain edg case where down the chain middlewar might want to access the file yile j on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 20t01 52 04z akats7 anoth option is to save c request to a variabl befor call c request withcontext ctx then in the defer function if c request multipartform nil we can reattach the multipartform to the origin request this way there won t be ani automat remov or pars if other middlewar handl the form correct this approach should work in http server go http github com golang go blob 40b3c0e58a0ae8dec4684a009bf3806769e0fc41 src net http server go l2102 the servehttp method is call first which invok the gin handler middlewar and then finishrequest is call which remov the temporari file\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"id\": \"b3dbc649c958ce01\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.29315551718650174, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.0808552359807168, \"vector_similarity\": 0.78852284, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 27213, \"chunk_count\": 18, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:09\", \"token_count\": 9176, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"    *   [https://github.com/golang/go/issues/71382](https://github.com/golang/go/issues/71382)\\n\\n    *   [https://github.com/golang/go/issues/74455](https://github.com/golang/go/issues/74455)\\n\\n*   **Bryan Boreham** questioned the relevance to OpenTelemetry, to which Damien clarified it's for instrumenting file uploads via the HTTP server.\\n\\n*   The discussion revolved around implementing an automatic cleanup mechanism for these temporary files. Proposed solutions included:\\n\\n    *   Option 1: `c.Request.MultipartForm.RemoveAll()`\\n\\n    *   Option 2: Leave it to the user to decide (\\\"whoever uses it is responsible for cleanup\\\")\\n\\n    *   Option 3: Provide a configurable option with a default.\\n\\n*   Damien suggested starting with automatic deletion without an explicit option, adding one only if a strong need arises. The notes from the agenda suggested starting with default behavior of removal, waiting for user interest to add configuration, and empowering component owners to make this decision.\\n\\n*   Tyler acknowledged that the instrumentation is responsible for cleanup and that this issue needs to be addressed.\\n\\n**3. Long-seen Code Owners/Triagers Check-in**\\n\\n*   **Damien Mathieu** reported that Chengzhen (Scorpion Knives), a triager and code owner for otelzap and otelecho, has had no GitHub activity since February and is the sole owner for otelecho.\\n\\n*   Damien pinged Chengzhen on Slack today and will wait a couple of weeks for a response. If there's no response, he plans to propose moving Chengzhen to Emeritus status due to inactivity.\\n\\n**4. Robert Pająk's PR (Parsing Algorithm)**\\n\\n*   **Robert Pająk** asked Tyler if his PR ([sdk/log: Fix AddAttributes, SetAttributes, SetBody on Record to not mutate input #7403](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/pull/7403)) needed Tyler's specific review or if another approval would suffice to unblock it.\\n\\n*   **Tyler Yahn** encouraged others to review and stated that the project shouldn't be blocked waiting for him, though he would try to review it within a few days.\\n\\n*   **David Ashpole** offered to review the PR. The goal is to merge it into the current milestone.\\n\\n**5. David Ashpole's PRs (Metrics SDK Optimizations)**\\n\\n*   **David Ashpole** provided an update on his histogram reservoir optimization PR. He explained that fixing a race condition initially worsened performance, making it equivalent to using a lock. The new approach involves one lock per measurement instead of one for the whole reservoir, resulting in a 3x-4x performance improvement. The PR is now much simpler and mostly involves concurrent safety testing.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"http github com golang go issu 71382 http github com golang go issu 71382 http github com golang go issu 74455 http github com golang go issu 74455 bryan boreham question the relev to opentelemetri to which damien clarifi it s for instrument file upload via the http server the discuss revolv around implement an automat cleanup mechan for these temporari file propos solut includ option 1 c request multipartform removeal option 2 leav it to the user to decid whoever us it is respons for cleanup option 3 provid a configur option with a default damien suggest start with automat delet without an explicit option ad one onli if a strong need aris the note from the agenda suggest start with default behavior of remov wait for user interest to add configur and empow compon owner to make this decis tyler acknowledg that the instrument is respons for cleanup and that this issu need to be address 3 long seen code owner triager check in damien mathieu report that chengzhen scorpion knife a triager and code owner for otelzap and otelecho ha had no github activ sinc februari and is the sole owner for otelecho damien ping chengzhen on slack today and will wait a coupl of week for a respons if there s no respons he plan to propos move chengzhen to emeritus status due to inact 4 robert paj ą k s pr pars algorithm robert paj ą k ask tyler if his pr sdk log fix addattribut setattribut setbodi on record to not mutat input 7403 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go pull 7403 need tyler s specif review or if anoth approv would suffic to unblock it tyler yahn encourag other to review and state that the project shouldn t be block wait for him though he would tri to review it within a few day david ashpol offer to review the pr the goal is to merg it into the current mileston 5 david ashpol s pr metric sdk optim david ashpol provid an updat on his histogram reservoir optim pr he explain that fix a race condit initi worsen perform make it equival to use a lock the new approach involv one lock per measur instead of one for the whole reservoir result in a 3x 4x perform improv the pr is now much simpler and most involv concurr safeti test\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"873e60b08a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"id\": \"88ce72df6cb6f6c4\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\":